{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And the meaning of 'now I know.'</b> I explained it in the section of Shemot, in the verse 'and they say to me, what is his name.'" "<b>And the sense of 'for in the matter.'</b> On account of the matter in which the Egyptians acted presumptuously against the people of Israel. And so he stated above, 'I know that YHWH is greater than all the Elohim' — YHWH, who executes judgment because they enslaved them with crushing labor. And so it is written, 'for you know that they dealt presumptuously against them' (Nehemiah 9:10), like a man who carries out his will presumptuously. And it is already written, 'for I know his afflictions, and I will come down to deliver him from the hand of Egypt' (above 3:7–8)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:35:31.330276370Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}